# Markdown is not committed by default.
#
# Markdown is ignored wholesale so that notes and scratch documents cannot be published by an
# absent-minded `git add .`. Publishing a document is then a deliberate act with a visible
# negation below it, which is a thing a reviewer can see.
#
# CLAUDE.md is deliberately NOT negated. It is working instructions, not documentation.
*.md
!README.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!CHANGELOG.md

# Agent instructions, same reasoning as CLAUDE.md above. Ignored here rather than relying on a
# global ignore, which is not present in someone else's checkout.
.claude/

# Private tooling lives in `bin/`; only `tools/` is shared. Ignored on this side as well, so a
# stray copy cannot be committed from a checkout that has one.
/bin/

/target/
**/target/
node_modules/
.env
logs/

# Scratch directories used by the test harness when comparing against upstream.
/tmp/

# parse-server log output from spec runs (its `logsFolder` in spec/helper.js).
test_logs/
__pycache__/
